iftop-web for Debian
====================

Two services are installed, enabled and started:

 iftop-collector  runs iftop-json as the _iftop-collector user (with only the
                  CAP_NET_RAW and CAP_NET_ADMIN capabilities), writes the
                  latest snapshot to /run/iftop-collector/live.json (tmpfs)
                  and the history to /var/lib/iftop-collector/iftop.db.
 iftop-web        runs the web interface under gunicorn as the _iftop-web
                  user, on http://127.0.0.1:8000/ by default.

Both read /etc/iftop-web/config.toml. Restart them after changing it:

  systemctl restart iftop-collector iftop-web


First steps
-----------

1. Create a user. There is no default account:

     iftop-web-user add alice

2. Choose the interface. By default iftop picks the first running one:

     interfaces = ["eth0"]

3. Open http://127.0.0.1:8000/ on the server, or through an SSH tunnel:

     ssh -L 8000:127.0.0.1:8000 server


Listening on other addresses
----------------------------

Plain HTTP is only allowed on localhost; iftop-web refuses to start
otherwise. Either:

 * give it a certificate, readable by _iftop-web:

     [web]
     bind = "0.0.0.0:8443"
     certfile = "/etc/iftop-web/cert.pem"
     keyfile = "/etc/iftop-web/key.pem"

   Port 443 works too; the service may bind ports below 1024.

 * or put a TLS-terminating reverse proxy in front, and set

     [web]
     bind = "127.0.0.1:8000"
     insecure_http = true
     proxy_fix = true

   proxy_fix makes the login rate limit see the clients' addresses instead of
   the proxy's.


Files
-----

 /etc/iftop-web/config.toml            configuration
 /run/iftop-collector/live.json        latest snapshot, rewritten every 2 s;
                                       on tmpfs, so it never touches the disk
 /run/iftop-collector/recent.db        the last hour of per-sample totals, for
                                       the minute and 5-minute charts (tmpfs)
 /var/lib/iftop-collector/iftop.db     traffic history (SQLite, readable by
                                       everyone), written every flush_interval
                                       seconds (60 by default, to spare flash
                                       storage); see also [retention]
 /var/lib/iftop-web/users.db           users (scrypt password hashes)
 /var/lib/iftop-web/secret_key         signs session cookies; created on first
                                       start. Deleting it logs everybody out.

Purging the package removes /var/lib/iftop-collector and /var/lib/iftop-web.
The system users are kept.

/usr/share/doc/iftop-web/README.md describes the web interface and its API.
